      ":question/problem": "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n(q-1)y=4\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=q-1,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nq-1=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-1 & =0 \\\\ q & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
